The Leleki Union of Ukrainians of Crete is a Ukrainian community organisation founded on the island of Crete in 2022. The Union brings Ukrainians together, helps preserve the Ukrainian language, culture and traditions, and builds a Ukrainian educational and cultural environment.

One of its key areas of work is mutual support and humanitarian aid. The Union helps people facing hardship, especially Ukrainians and refugees who were forced to leave Ukraine because of the war and found shelter on Crete.

Leleki also takes part in humanitarian initiatives supporting Ukraine, Ukrainian soldiers, hospitals and medical facilities.

Children and young people are at the centre of the Union’s work: the Ukrainian Saturday school, cultural and educational events, creative projects, and keeping the new generation connected with Ukraine.

The Union also represents Ukrainian culture on Crete and helps Greek society get to know Ukraine, its history, traditions and contemporary culture.

## Mission

To unite Ukrainians on Crete, preserve Ukrainian identity, develop culture and education, help those in need and support Ukraine.

## Main areas of work

- uniting the Ukrainian community and mutual support;
- humanitarian aid for Ukrainians and refugees;
- support for Ukrainian soldiers;
- support for hospitals and medical facilities in Ukraine;
- charity initiatives and fundraisers;
- Ukrainian education and the Saturday school;
- cultural, educational and creative events;
- preserving the Ukrainian language, culture and traditions;
- promoting Ukrainian culture on Crete;
- creating a Ukrainian environment for children, young people and adults.

