Need reliable information about living in Greece? Not sure how to get temporary protection, which documents you need, or where to go with a specific question? Come to the office of the United Ukrainian Diaspora in Greece in Athens.

## We can help you find up-to-date, reliable information on

- temporary protection in Greece;
- documents and official procedures;
- social issues;
- healthcare and education;
- access to public services;
- other questions about life in Greece.

Don’t rely on information from random chats and social media. Rules and procedures change, so it’s important to check information against official sources — we’ll help you find your way.

## How to find us

- Address: 4 Feron Street, 104 34 Athens (near Victoria Square).
- Opening hours: 10:00–17:00.
- Phone: +30 697 653 3390, +30 210 821 9950.
- Email: ukrdiasporagr@gmail.com.

The centre also hosts Greek and English conversation clubs, workshops and community meetups.

